    "title": "Marshalls confirms every single US store is CLOSED for 24 hours in massive shopping blackout",
    "text": "MARSHALLS customers must get all of their shopping done before the chain closes all of its stores for an entire day. The popular chain is closing this Easter Sunday, alongside others like Goodwill, so shoppers won’t be able to access a key part of the business. Sign up for the Money newsletter Thank you! Marshalls will close all of its stores for Easter SundayCredit: Alamy Marshalls will close on Easter Sunday, which falls on April 5, so shoppers are advised to get to stores beforehand to avoid delays. Easter Sunday is one of the main holidays celebrated in the United States, and many retailers close to observe it. Other major federal holidays celebrated annually include New Year’s Day, Thanksgiving and Christmas. Marshalls’ website will be running on April 5, so shoppers can still browse for their next buy. But any purchases made online won’t be processed until the following day, which could impact shipping times. This is the same for other retailers who have confirmed they will close on Easter Sunday. Aldi and Costco will close their doors on Easter Sunday. Aldi shoppers will not be able to enter any of its stores across the country, and Costco warehouses will be closed. Most read in Money The United States Postal Service (USPS) will also freeze most of its services on April 5. Some retailers may operate limited hours, so shoppers will only be able to access certain stores for a specific time. What are Costco’s holiday closures? New Year’s Day Easter Sunday Memorial Day Independence Day Labor Day Thanksgiving Day Christmas Day To find out, shoppers should search for the locator tool online for the store they want to visit. This should tell them if the spot is open on Easter Sunday. Comments",
